Concern: a run with no command line names the adapter its prefill steps load, before any engine exists
Upstream: not-submitted
A trainer that drives radiance through an interface of its own -- r97train's loss pass -- has no
command line for radiance to parse and no Engine to load an adapter into: it opens a forward
driver, and the driver opens the engines. lora/preload.h is how such a run reaches the loader: it
names the adapter at startup, every engine started afterwards joins it to its startup adapters, and
its prefill steps run through it. Everything after that is --lora's own path: read_targets(),
lora_start() and the slot table. The named adapter fills cfg_.prefill_lora, the field the earlier
training patch 0104-prefill-lora.patch adds, so this patch is applied after it.

